  "sourceFindings": [
    {
      "path": "driver-session.js",
      "finding": "close seals and aborts, then awaits original loop/control/snapshotted replies. The protocol-dispose stage is assigned only after that join; confirmStopped is entered only if protocol.dispose resolves."
    },
    {
      "path": "v2-driver-backend.js + v2-driver-native.js",
      "finding": "The actual V2 backend delegates dispose to native.dispose. Native dispose sets closed, aborts shutdown, latches cleanupUnknown if activeOperations>0, then throws cleanup_unknown if the latch is set. This method performs no additional native HTTP request, child adoption, child census or stop confirmation."
    },
    {
      "path": "v2-driver-native.js",
      "finding": "The latch may originate from a prior cleanup_unknown or native_read_cleanup_unknown error, a rejected per-operation wire.dispose, or an active-operation observation at close. It intentionally remains latched even if subsequent tracked work settles."
    },
    {
      "path": "v2-native-cut.js",
      "finding": "A failed after-log/after-session sibling is aborted and joined with Promise.allSettled. Any unknown-cleanup rejection wins over the first ordinary failure. The existing failure producer publishes both the original first reason and finalReason after this translation/join."
    },
    {
      "path": "passive-diagnostics.ts",
      "finding": "The exact current projector validates and retains original reason, stage, elapsedMs, deadlineExpired and aborted, but drops producer finalReason. The resulting receipt cannot distinguish the initial transport failure from a later native_read_cleanup_unknown propagated out of the cut."
    },
    {
      "path": "v2-execution-transport.js",
      "finding": "Per-operation disposal aborts controllers and joins pending/io under the existing finite bound; nonempty sets or expired join retain unknown. The new receipt contains neither the relevant set counts nor the concrete cancellation/disposal rejection reason."
    }
  ],
